  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "Ed25519 is a high-performance elliptic-curve digital signature scheme instantiated on the Twisted Edwards curve over the prime field GF(2^255-19), offering approximately 128 bits of security with deterministic signing and compact 64-byte signatures. Designed by Bernstein et al., it is engineered to resist side-channel attacks through constant-time implementation properties and avoids the weak-nonce vulnerabilities that affect ECDSA. Ed25519 is standardised in RFC 8032 and is widely deployed across blockchain networks, SSH authentication (OpenSSH), and decentralised identity systems.",
